        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A <strong class="text-white">point of use water heater</strong> is the right fix for one far sink or one spot the main heater never reached. Choose a mini-tank when the flow is high but brief and you only have a standard outlet, and a small tankless unit when the flow is low and you never want it to run dry.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Run the temperature-rise math against your winter water before buying anything tankless, pipe the relief valve on any tank, and do not ask a point of use heater to run a shower in a cold climate. If the whole house waits for hot water, recirculation or a better central heater is the real answer.
          </p>
        </div>

